\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\,{e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x)(\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{2})(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\,{e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\,{e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{4}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\int x\\,{e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}}{2}-(\\frac{x\\,{e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{4}+D) \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\frac{x\\,{e}^{2x+2}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{4}-D \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{4}(2{x}^{2}-2x+11)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-D.$ \n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{4}(2{x}^{2}-2x+11)]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{2(1)+2}}{4}(2(1)^{2}-2(1)+11))-(\\frac{{e}^{2(0)+2}}{4}(2(0)^{2}-2(0)+11)) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4}}{4}(2-2+11)-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{4}(0-0+11) \\\\  & =\\frac{11{e}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{11{e}^{2}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{11{e}^{4}-11{e}^{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534472 true] [17592186290228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290229 13194139534472 true] [17592186290228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290230 13194139534472 true] [17592186290228 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534472 true] [17592186290228 1041 "field-1" 13194139534472 true] [17592186290228 1104 #edb/ref 17592186290229 13194139534472 true] [17592186290228 1110 #uuid "80bfeab6-b03f-5a2a-a2ed-a9d231928089" 13194139534472 true] [17592186290229 1034 "\\frac{11e^4-11e^2}{4}" 13194139534472 true] [17592186290229 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 1319413